## 📋 Spec Analysis

```
Feature name: SmartQC — Test Case Generator Full Pipeline
Feature type: Combined (Web UI + API + Mobile)
Actors: QC Engineer, Tester, QA Manager

Main flows (Happy Paths):
1. User uploads a valid .md spec → skill analyzes → generates test cases + report template
2. User pastes spec text → same pipeline executes
3. User specifies optional inputs (env, platform, coverage) → output is scoped accordingly
4. Generation is cut off mid-run → skill stops cleanly and outputs resume instruction
5. Sensitive data detected in spec → masked silently, notice prepended to output

Business rules:
- Input must be a .md spec file (uploaded or pasted)
- Skill auto-detects: feature type, platforms, main flows, edge cases, risk areas
- Output always has 2 artifacts: test case document + report template
- TC ID format: TC-[MODULE]-[NUM]
- Priority auto-assigned: Critical / Major / Minor per defined rules
- Version bump: patch (same spec re-run), minor (updated spec), major (rewrite)
- Security masking: 7 sensitive data categories, always masked before processing
- Retry: max 3 attempts, fallback to partial output with resume flag
- Language: match spec language; English for mixed

Data entities involved:
- Spec file (input), Test Case Document (output), Report Template (output), Version Log

Dependencies:
- Claude Project platform, Claude Sonnet model, SKILL.md instructions

Ambiguities:
- No explicit SLA defined for generation time ("2–5 minutes" is aspirational, not contractual)
- "Roll back to v1.0" implies version files are persisted, but Claude Projects have no persistent storage — unclear how this works across sessions
- "GitHub push with each generation" mentioned in section 9 but no GitHub integration is described in the skill itself
- Retry mechanism (section 8) references a 30s timeout — who enforces this? The Claude API or the skill wrapper?
- "Does not store conversation history beyond current session" conflicts with "roll back to v1.0" feature

Risk areas:
🔴 Security masking — if masking fails, PII/secrets leak into output
🔴 Incomplete output handling — if cutoff detection fails, half-written TCs go to QC
🔴 Version rollback — depends on session persistence that may not exist in Claude Projects
🟡 Spec quality dependency — vague input produces vague output with no clear error
🟡 Multi-module specs — TC ID prefix assignment may collide or be ambiguous
```

